  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 150 AM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nHigh pressure behind Friday's cold front will continue to usher \ndrier and cooler air across S TX today, which will lead to highs in \nthe lower 70s. Strong gusty north winds this morning along the \ncoastline and the islands, will diminish through this afternoon, \nbecoming light tonight. Skies are expected to clear tonight and with \nthe dry airmass in place and light winds, efficient radiational \ncooling will be maximized, allowing temperatures to drop into the \n50s most areas to low 60s along the coast. Light winds are forecast \nto gradually shift to the northeast and east on Sunday, thus \nbeginning to usher warmer air from the gulf waters back into S TX. \nTemperatures will gradually increase through the week with highs \napproaching the 90s by mid week.\n\nGale force winds across the coastal waters will diminish from west \nto east throughout the day. The Gale Warning is in effect until 7 AM \nfor the bays and until 1 PM for the Coastal Waters, and will be \nreplaced with a Small Craft Advisory for the afternoon. Winds may \ndrop below advisory levels by late afternoon, but seas will take \nlonger to subside, thus maintaining advisory conditions due to the \nseas through this evening.\n\nAnother concern continues to be the potential for coastal flooding \nand a high rip current risk. Due to a more north direction, the \ntides have not increased so far. However, winds are forecast to veer \nto the northeast throughout the day. The more northeast component \nwill be more conducive for minor coastal flooding. Wind speeds will \ndecrease but remain at 15-20 knots this evening. These northeast \nwinds combined with swell periods of around 8 seconds will likely \nlead to minor coastal flooding during times of high tide this \nevening and overnight. The Coastal Flood Advisory remains in effect \nthrough Sunday morning. In addition, the long period swells will be \nconducive for a moderate to high rip current risk today and tonight. \n\nAs for any rain chances for the upcoming week, most areas will \nremain dry with very low chances. There are periods where there is a \nlow chance along the Southern Coastal Bend and low to medium chance \nacross the Coastal Waters.",
